        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T19:12:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still suggest __default because it\u0027s short and descriptive. If it\u0027s not liked, maybe we can simply use \u0027__weak\u0027.\n\nWe should optimize names for normal \u0026 experienced developers. (Imagine how many times you will grep for \u0027__default\u0027 v.s. \u0027__overridable_default\u0027?) These\u0027re pretty simple keywords. Once a new contributor looks it up, it\u0027ll  quickly make sense.",
      "parentUuid": "c7e9aba3_08cf2e90",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
