    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "570c8727_ed7b1683",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T19:17:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think __default is fine.\n\n__weak would be a misnomer, as in my plugin work right now, it is using it\u0027s own custom attribute, that while provides a weak symbol, also does a lot more (including name mangling).",
      "parentUuid": "71ba7746_2edb8fc7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5166919_e2133855",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T20:23:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think __default is too general or broad. I don\u0027t think we need to optimize for character count. I think the few extra character makes it easier to follow exactly what is happening\n\n__override_default is much more descriptive and targeted.",
      "parentUuid": "570c8727_ed7b1683",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac14f015_eaea103a",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
