    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b19301e2_c6e14733",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T20:49:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "which is why we rolled around to __overridable_default...  If you are looking for less characters we could change that to __overridable_base.  Either one of these works for me.",
      "parentUuid": "ac14f015_eaea103a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8aeae1c6_46d38f8e",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T22:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think __default is too general or broad\n\nYes, \u0027default\u0027 is broad but if it\u0027s placed in front of a symbol, it just works right:\n\n  __default int foo(void) {...}\n\nI imagine people will read it \u0027default (definition of) foo\u0027. override_default can read two ways (as Jack pointed out). The problem is the unintended way (\u0027overriding default\u0027) actually gives the opposite meaning.\n\n\u003e which is why we rolled around to __overridable_default \n\nSomething default (default config/size/color/etc.) is always overridable. So, overridable_default is redundant. \u0027Default\u0027 implies it\u0027s meant to be overridden.",
      "parentUuid": "b19301e2_c6e14733",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e2f5a21_07d923c4",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T22:26:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One could interpret __default as the default attribute that is applied to functions when there nothing else to annotate. If could be a default annotation.\n\n__overridable_default or __overridable_base or even __virtual_base give more context.",
      "parentUuid": "8aeae1c6_46d38f8e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f70d49d34196fbbddfb583badec6eedf7d0b20ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "953cdd14_6290641b",
        "filename": "include/common.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-29T22:37:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e One could interpret __default as the default attribute that is applied to functions when there nothing else to annotate. If could be a default annotation.\n\nOnce I finish the GCC plugin, it will error at compile time if someone attempts this without an appropriate __overridable declaration.\n\n\u003e __overridable_default or __overridable_base or even __virtual_base give more context.\n\nthe *_base names aren\u0027t really clear that this is a default implementation (sort of makes sense, but it takes some thinking about).\n\n__overridable_default is OK, but is lengthy. Of course, people can define snippets in their editors to solve this (so only a minor cosmetic issue).\n\nI still think __default is not all that bad.\n\nIn any of the above cases, someone not familiar with the mechanism will end up code-searching the name, finding the comment here on how to use it, and will become familiar with it. So honestly I think this naming thing is the least of our concerns.",
      "parentUuid": "6e2f5a21_07d923c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 17
      },
